Looking at E9 carefully:

- ORD-00143: `created_at=80` (well before t=300 baseline, and before the deploy at t=436) — this was already bad before the deploy.
- ORD-00854: `created_at=437` (after deploy at t=436) — bad after deploy.
- ORD-00859: `created_at=440` (after deploy at t=436) — bad after deploy.

ORD-00143 was created at t=80, meaning the bad extraction predates the v1.1 deploy. This suggests the invoice text itself contains wrong VAT figures (bad_input), OR invoice-agent was already extracting incorrectly before the deploy. I need to check ORD-00143's invoice text more carefully and also check whether ORD-00143's ledger row was written recently (post-deploy) or long ago.

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT l.order_id, l.synced_at, i.created_at FROM ledger l JOIN invoices i ON l.order_id = i.order_id WHERE l.order_id IN ('ORD-00143','ORD-00854','ORD-00859')",
      "why": "Check when each bad ledger row was synced vs when the invoice was created, to determine if ORD-00143's ledger entry is old (pre-deploy bad_input) or newly written, and whether the two post-deploy rows confirm the bad_deploy hypothesis."
    },
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT order_id, invoice_text FROM orders WHERE order_id IN ('ORD-00143','ORD-00854','ORD-00859')",
      "why": "Read the full invoice texts to check whether the VAT figures in the source documents are already wrong (bad_input) or whether invoice-agent is misextracting correct source data."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [],
  "summary": "ORD-00143 predates the deploy (created_at=80) suggesting a possible second independent cause; investigating ledger sync times and raw invoice texts to separate bad_input from bad_deploy."
}
```
